ROUND-145 QCO WIND RECIPROCAL ROUTING CANDIDATE (2026-09-21; base
683f58206d06a640e89c0a6e6b1786d00e102001; measured candidate
c08132745455b382c610a21d94c20eeabb4be576): HELD.  The source-exact
developed-state boundary closes, but Decision 43 and Decision 45 refuse the
trajectory.  No physics from this patch is present at the round-145 final tip.

COMPILED STATEMENT.  The record build materialises r1_hu_0/r1_hv_0 in
domain.f90:212-215, constructs QCO r3u/r3v with surface-area weighting in
domqco.f90:160-182,188-218, and adds wind at stp2d.f90:249-250 as
tau*r1_hu_0/(1+r3u(Kbb)) and tau*r1_hv_0/(1+r3v(Kbb)).  The candidate reuses
the shared `_nemo_ws_qco_stage_faces(..., include_reciprocals=True)` outputs
for both the already-landed momentum face thickness and these wind inverse
depths; it adds no formula or configuration selector.

LOCAL PROOF.  From NEMO's admitted day-180 entry through the production-JIT
step, the live incoming slow forcing becomes BIT for both U (580 wet cells)
and V (570 wet cells).  The callback/plain state is BIT across 198,956 cells
and 23 leaves.  A one-ULP inverse-depth plant changes the consumed boundary
and exits nonzero.  The remaining final U/V difference is 268/580 cells at
6.88214269644119e-22 and 247/570 at 8.470329472543003e-22 respectively; it is
downstream of the closed wind boundary.

TRAJECTORY VETO.  The certified 70-row kt1..10 comparison registers 58 moved
rows, no kt1 AT-BAR loss, and first-over-bar remains kt2 U/V.  Kt2 T/S/U/V are
unchanged; kt3 T/S worsen from 8.659373840202989e-7 / 7.027291104577671e-8 to
8.659374053365809e-7 / 7.027291815120407e-8.  Day-30 T rms worsens from
6.890431487825909e-5 to 6.890433793037169e-5 K and day-360 worsens from
1.1223571247843664e-2 to 1.1223669244045392e-2 K.  Day-240 improves only
8.12156487e-11 K.  Criteria 43(a) and 45(f) therefore fail.

BLAST RADIUS.  Recipe-derived resolution finds GYRE-zco and the generic
build_nemo_gyre_recipe card execute; the latter moves all 15 certified
